{"change_summary":"Completed the conservation remediation on top of the existing budget-ledger plumbing. Active closed-system N/C budget checks now pass because the daily biology and nitrogen-cycle paths conserve tracked mass under normal operation: plant/algae growth now debit DIC, plant respiration and algae respiration/grazing route biomass back into dissolved organic pools, decomposer and nitrifier growth/decay move N/C explicitly between dissolved and biomass pools, and water changes now keep the dissolved-feed-residue mirror aligned with DOC/DON export. Canonical total-helper coverage is now guarded by a structural test that compares the helper component labels against serialized element-bearing state paths, and the broader algae/event/shrimp regression fixtures were rebalanced so the full `tank_core` suite still reflects the conserved nutrient pathways.","outstanding_risks":["The canonical helper coverage guard is structural but still heuristic: if a future explicit element-bearing field uses a new naming pattern or lives in an empty-by-default collection, the coverage test must be extended to recognize it.","Shrimp lifecycle transitions still model biomass through counts rather than explicit N/C transfer pools; if future budget-ledger work needs strict conservation across spawning, hatching, maturation, or mortality, those paths will need the same explicit bookkeeping treatment.","`dissolved_feed_residue_g_total` remains an excluded bookkeeping mirror of dissolved organics. Any future system or action that exports or transforms DOC/DON must keep that mirror synchronized or clogging diagnostics will drift from the canonical totals."],"steps":[{"description":"Audit the budget-ledger implementation against the pending amendments, identify the remaining mass leaks in active biology/nitrogen-cycle paths, and confirm which regressions were still tautological or missing mirror coverage.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Implement the conservation fixes so active closed-system ticks stay balanced: ensure plant/algae growth consumes DIC, route plant/algae/shrimp/microfauna biomass losses into tracked pools, keep microbial growth/decay element-explicit, and preserve the dissolved-feed-residue mirror through water changes.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Strengthen regression coverage by converting the closed-system budget tests to an active biological state, adding a structural canonical-helper coverage test, extending water-change coverage for non-zero residue, and adjusting long-horizon algae/event/shrimp fixtures to match the conserved mass pathways.","order":3,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Run focused and full-package validation to confirm the budget fixes and the downstream behavior regressions both pass cleanly.","order":4,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo test -p tank_core --test budget_tracking` passed (7 tests, including active 24-tick N/C conservation, water-change export/residue tracking, zero-cost disabled-path gating, and structural canonical-helper coverage).","`cargo test -p tank_core --test water_change_mass_balance` passed (8 tests).","`cargo test -p tank_core` passed across the full `tank_core` suite.","`cargo clippy -p tank_core -- -D warnings` passed."]}